# Claude Security -- suggested patch for F1: Image build/sign/release pipeline does not restrict the ref to main's ancestry, letting any pushed tag or dispatched branch become the repo-signed :1 image
# Applies to revision da3f5ff15143 (the revision these patches were built against).
#
# Verified by a panel of agents: an independent verifier reviewed this
# change against the finding, and a second, fresh reviewer challenged the
# diff for an attack path it opens, or a route it leaves open to the
# finding's exploit. The patch was written only because the panel stated
# all three of these with confidence:
#   - the change is highly targeted to this finding: git diff --cached --name-status shows only .github/workflows/publish.yml; a single hunk adding one gate step that mirrors publish-ios-channel.yml, no other line touched
#   - the change introduces no new security vulnerability: the gate only adds a fail-closed refusal using GitHub's $GITHUB_SHA (a 40-hex env var, not ${{ }} interpolation) and origin/main from the authenticated checkout, so no command/expression injection and no new surface
#   - beyond closing the finding, the change does not alter the code's behaviour or the inputs it accepts: the only change to accepted input is turning away off-main refs at the publish sinks, which is the intended fix; legitimate on-main tags and dispatches still build/push/sign/release unchanged
#
# NOTE: no project test of the patched code was run. The claim that
# behaviour is unchanged rests on review of the change and its callers,
# not on a test run -- weigh it accordingly before applying.
#
# publish.yml built, pushed, cosign-signed and released whatever commit any v* tag or dispatched branch pointed at, with no check it was on main; the patch adds a fail-closed 'git merge-base --is-ancestor "$GITHUB_SHA" origin/main' gate right after checkout, mirroring publish-ios-channel.yml, so an off-main ref is refused before any publish/sign/release step.
# Tests run: none possible: no Go toolchain on this box, and the Go suite does not exercise .github/workflows; verifier probe (not a project test): python3 yaml.safe_load(publish.yml) parsed, gate confirmed at step index 1 before setup-go, go test, build-push, cosign sign and the release
#
# Apply, from the repository root:  git apply CLAUDE-SECURITY-20260926-213603/patches/F1.patch
#
diff --git a/.github/workflows/publish.yml b/.github/workflows/publish.yml
index 0c552e8..36ae324 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/publish.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/publish.yml
@@ -32,6 +32,18 @@ jobs:
         with:
           fetch-depth: 0 # tags, for the major on a manual run
 
+      # Only a commit on the protected main branch may be built, pushed,
+      # signed and released. A v* tag or a manual dispatch can point at any
+      # commit (main's branch protection does not extend to tags), so refuse
+      # anything that is not on main's ancestry before it reaches the registry
+      # push, the keyless cosign signing or the GitHub Release — the same gate
+      # publish-ios-channel.yml applies before it trusts a tag.
+      - name: Refuse a ref that is not on main's ancestry
+        run: |
+          set -euo pipefail
+          git merge-base --is-ancestor "$GITHUB_SHA" origin/main || {
+            echo "::error::commit $GITHUB_SHA is not on main's ancestry; refusing to publish"; exit 1; }
+
       # A broken build never becomes a published image.
       - uses: actions/setup-go@40f1582b2485089dde7abd97c1529aa768e1baff # v5
         with:
